{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to plants classified VAI 1049 and 943 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D4", "D5"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the etomidate shortage on 2022-10-05 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E39", "D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hospira, Inc. plant (FEI 1021343) that manufactures etomidate was classified VAI on 2019-11-21, 1049 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D4", "E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hikma Farmaceutica (Portugal) S.A. plant (FEI 3002807173) that manufactures etomidate was classified VAI on 2020-03-06, 943 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D5", "E28"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Both plants received subsequent VAI classifications after the shortage posting, on 2023-02-03 and 2023-04-21.",
      "cites": ["D6", "D7", "E29", "E30"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 7.6 days of etomidate 2 mg/mL 10 mL vials on hand while Corvale General has 17 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 70 vials from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would give Corvale East 11 days on hand while Corvale General retains 14 days.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    }
  ]
}
